{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/ja1sjq5s","slide":10,"text":"Replace simulation adapters with\nmonitoring, deployment, and\nnotification integrations.\n\nPersist incident records in\nproduction-grade shared storage.","textPreview":"Replace simulation adapters with | monitoring, deployment, and | notification integrations. |  | Persist incident records in | production...","textChars":149,"textLines":6,"bbox":[872,258,270,160]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/w7atovmh","slide":10,"text":"Expected operational value must be validated with a pilot. The prototype demonstrates the workflow and its safety controls, not performance claims.","textPreview":"Expected operational value must be validated with a pilot. The prototype demonstrates the workflow and its safety controls, not performan...","textChars":147,"textLines":1,"bbox":[120,552,980,44]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/3i0qn3","slide":10,"text":"Say: The immediate users are the people running incidents. The product gives them a shared evidence trail, a concrete approval record and a durable ledger. For scale, the simulation adapters map directly to real monitoring, deployment and notification systems. Any measurable improvement needs a real pilot, so we do not claim numbers here.\n\nVisual: Target user roles and a practical scale path. Include visible disclosure on unvalidated impact.\n\nLayout: One narrative: who benefits, then how it scales."}
